.TH "RPMSORT" "8" "27 October 2022" "" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
rpmsort - Sort input by RPM Package Manager (RPM) versioning.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]rpmsort\f[R] \f[I]FILES\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[B]rpmsort\f[R] sorts the input files, and writes a sorted list to
standard out - like sort(1), but aware of RPM versioning.
.PP
If \[aq]-\[aq] is given as an argument, or no arguments are given,
versions are read from stdandard in and writen to standard out.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\f[B]\f[BI]$ echo -e `rpm-4.18.0-3.fc38.x86_64.0-1.fc38.x86_64' |
rpmsort
.PD 0
.P
.PD
rpm-4.18.0-1.fc38.x86_64
.PD 0
.P
.PD
rpm-4.18.0-3.fc38.x86_64\f[B]\f[R]
